-- title:
--   Locally norm-transported full level structure on a rigidified curve
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r \neq r$ (`hrr`), $N$ is a nonzero natural number with $r \nmid N$ (`hrN`), $\bar r \nmid N$ (`hrbarN`) and $N$ squarefree (`hN`).
--
--   **Coefficients.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi \in \mathcal O$ is irreducible (`hπ`), $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next, $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $F_r$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), with that ideal maximal (`hOnr_max`), such that every element satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $F_r x \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is given, with `hvdet` asserting that $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli.** $a, b \in \mathbb Q$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite ($0 < a$ or $0 < b$) and, at a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$, is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies above $r$ or $\bar r$ (`hB`); $\Lambda$ is a maximal $\mathbb Z$-order in it (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a point map $\mathrm{pt}$ is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves of level $N$ (`h𝒳`: isomorphism-invariance, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points, and the universal property). Further, $n \geq 3$ with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N) = 1$; $M \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{ptF}$ is a fine moduli space for fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`); a group $G$ acts on $M$ through $\rho$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ realising the level-twisting action (`hρ`). A forgetful morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hp`) is $G$-invariant (`hρp`) and compatible with the point maps (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \neq r, \bar r$, $\mathcal Y_\ell \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{ptT}_\ell$ is a coarse moduli space for curves with extra $\ell$-level (`h𝒴`), and degeneracy morphisms $d_0, d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) realise forgetting the $\ell$-level (`hd₀`) and passing to an $\ell$-level isogeny quotient (`hd₁`). Endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`harf`, `harbarf`) induce the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side.** $a_1, b_1 \in \mathbb Q$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`); $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`); $n_1$ is a finite-adelic unit in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); $\iota_0$ is an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); $v$ is a height-one prime containing $r$ (`hv`). The subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ is the group of units integral away from $v$ with respect to $R_1$ (`hΓt`). Families $s_\ell$ of global units and $sf_\ell$ of finite-adelic units, indexed by the primes $\ell \neq r, \bar r$, satisfy `hs`: at each place not containing $r$ the component of $sf_\ell$ is $s_\ell \otimes 1$, at each place containing $r$ it is $1$, the product of the diagonal image of the scalar $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}\,\Lambda_1\,(R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})\,\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; $\Gamma_{t,\ell}$ is the intersection of $\Gamma_t$ with its conjugate by $s_\ell$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`). Finally $\mathbb Z \subseteq \Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`) and $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathbb Z_{r^2} \times \mathbb Z_{r^2}$ is an order coordinate in the sense of `IsOrderCoord` (`hcoord`): additive, unital, multiplicative for the twisted Witt-vector rule, injective, with dense image and the prescribed trace identity.
--
--   **The base object and its uniformisation package.** Over the residue ring $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ there are a fake elliptic curve $A_0$ of level $N$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of $A_0$ in two variables with $A_0$ a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$ and $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`), endomorphism families $e, e'$ indexed by $\Gamma_t$ with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $\deg \gamma$. The hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4`, `hE5a`–`hE5e` and `hJOINTw` (summarised here) constitute the $\Gamma_t$-uniformisation package for $A_0$: each $(e\gamma, e'\gamma)$ is an $r^{\deg\gamma}$-isogeny pair preserving the level structure; the assignment $\gamma \mapsto e\gamma$ is multiplicative and sends rational integral scalars to the corresponding $\Lambda$-action, up to multiplication by powers of $r$, and conversely only scalars act by scalars; for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\mathbb Z_{r^2}$-action and uniformiser endomorphism of $X_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser with $E_0\varepsilon = r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; every full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ is moved by $e\gamma$ into its own $\Lambda$-orbit by labels satisfying the cocycle conditions modulo $n$; every $r$-power isogeny preserving the level of a fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field obtained from $A_0$ by base change comes from some $e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$; and the action extends to an order $R_2 \leq R_1$ with $r$-power denominators ($\mathrm{hR₂}$, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) by endomorphisms $\hat e$ over the base (`hê`) which are additive, $\Lambda$-equivariant and level-preserving, unital, multiplicative, restrict to the $\Lambda$-action on integers, satisfy $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x) = \mathrm{nrd}(x)$, are compatible with $e\gamma$ on $r$-power multiples of $\gamma$, and are simultaneously normalised by a single $g$ as above, the last also accommodating $\bar w$ and the composite $a_w \circ b_w$ in `hJOINTw`.
--
--   **The special formal module side.** $\iota : \mathbb Z_{r^2} \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a ring map, $\Phi$ is a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`), $MD$ is a moduli package over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and $\eta$ assigns to each rigidified $\Phi$-object over a ring an element of $MD$; `hη` (three clauses) states that on admissible objects over Noetherian rings $\eta$ separates exactly the isomorphism classes, is compatible with base change, and is locally surjective over a finite cover by basic opens. $E_0$ is an injective ring map from the centraliser attached to $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is comparable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ after scaling by a fixed power $r^m$ (`hE₀`).
--
--   **The Drinfeld dictionary.** $eD$ is a family of maps from the points of the functor $G(\mathcal O, MD)$ over Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent to the product of the functor corepresented by $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ with the Deligne-datum functor $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}$, natural (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), compatible with the first leg (`hfstD`), transporting the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $G$-points into the $\mathrm{vdet}$-twisted action on $\Omega$-data (`hGLD`), transporting $\pi$-translation into Frobenius twisting of the leg (`hPiD`), with $\pi$-translates always existing (`hPiexD`). Further, $\kappa : O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi) \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ factors the quotient map (`hκ`), and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny of formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules from $\Phi$ to $\kappa_*X_0$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). $P_0$ is a full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$. The data $A_{0w}$, $a_w, a_w', b_w, b_w', k_w$ with `hALw`, `hBSw`, `hBSwlev` and the displayed compatibilities exhibit $A_{0w}$ as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$ together with an $r^{k_w}$-isogeny back which preserves the level.
--
--   **The classifying map.** $\Xi$ assigns to each rigidified fake elliptic curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, relative to a leg $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$, a $G$-point of $MD$, subject to: `hΞleg`, the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist $F_r^{k}$ of $\psi$ when $B$ has only trivial idempotents; `hΞnat`, compatibility with pullbacks of rigidifications along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps; `hΞiso`, invariance under isomorphisms of the underlying curves equipped with the displayed comparison data on the reductions and on the auxiliary isogenies; and `hΞdef`, the explicit description: for connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent and any formal module structure $(X,\theta)$ on the curve via $\mathrm{coord}$, there are $j \leq 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ with $t.X = X$, which is a rigid transport of $\theta_0$ along $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ and $\varrho$ with exponent $j$, admissible for $\iota$ and the $(-j)$-th Frobenius twist of $\psi$, and $\Xi$ of the curve equals the $G$-point assembled from that twisted leg and $\eta(t)$.
--
--   Finally $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is given, with `heqΓ`: translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ corresponds, under $\Xi$, to acting by $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$ for some $c \in \mathbb Z$; `heqW`: an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ together with the displayed comparison data involving $a_w \circ b_w$ corresponds to acting by $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g_0^{-1}$; `hK1`–`hK4`: over connected Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent, every point of $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}$ is matched by a rigidified curve whose $\Xi$-image has the expected leg and is $g_0^{-1}$-twisted-equivalent to it (`hK1`), two such matches are isomorphic with comparison data (`hK2`), matches base-change along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps (`hK3`), and matches lift along a surjection $p : B \to B_0$ whose kernel squares to zero elementwise, compatibly with the twisted action (`hK4`); and `hC0e`, `hC0u`: over a connected Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, a rigidification relative to the leg twisted by $-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)$ together with a formal module structure admits a full level-$n$ structure which is a height-normalised level transport of $P_0$ (`IsNormLevelTransport`), and any two height-normalised level transports along the same rigidification have the same underlying section.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $B$ be a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent and whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, let $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, let $E$ be a fake elliptic curve of level $N$ over $B$ and let $\varrho$ be a rigidification of $E$ relative to the leg $F_r^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}\psi$. Then there exists a full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $E$ with the following property. For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B_c$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent and whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi_c : B \to B_c$, every fake elliptic curve $E_c$ of level $N$ over $B_c$ and morphism $g_c : E_c.A \to E.A$ exhibiting $E_c$ as the pullback of $E$ along $\varphi_c$ (as a group law with $\Lambda$-action and level datum), every rigidification $\varrho_c$ of $E_c$ relative to $\varphi_c \circ (F_r^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}\psi)$ which is the pullback of $\varrho$ along $\varphi_c$ and $g_c$, every full level-$n$ structure $P_c$ on $E_c$ whose section satisfies $P_c.P$ followed by $g_c$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\varphi_c)$ followed by $P_n.P$, and every formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_c$ over $B_c$ with formal coordinates $\theta_c$ making $E_c$ a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$: the structure $P_c$ is the height-normalised level transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho_c$, that is, `IsNormLevelTransport Fr θ₀ κ β₀ Φ ι coord P₀ ϱc Pc` holds. Unfolded, this last assertion says that there is a section $Q$ of $\varrho_c.Ab$ over $B_c/(\pi)$ with $Q$ followed by $\varrho_c.gA$ equal to the residue leg base change of $P_0.P$, together with a formal module structure on $E_c$ via $\mathrm{coord}$, an exponent $j \leq 1$ and a rigidified $\Phi$-object $t$ over $B_c$ with $t.X$ that formal module, which is a rigid transport of $\theta_0$ with exponent $j$ and admissible for $\iota$ and the $(-j)$-th Frobenius twist of the leg, such that the reduction modulo $\pi$ of $r^{t.n}\!\cdot\!P_c$ equals $Q$ followed by $\varrho_c.\varphi'$ and $\varrho_c.gb$.
--
--   The level-$n$ structure produced is thus characterised only through its base changes to connected Noetherian quotients and localisations; no clause asserts the transport property for $P_n$ over $B$ itself.
--
--   This is the level-structure step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the fake-elliptic-curve moduli problem: the $p$-adic rigidification dictionary produces curves over connected bases, and the statement equips a rigidified curve with a full level-$n$ structure that is, after any connected base change, the height-normalised transport of the fixed level structure $P_0$ on the base curve $A_0$. It is used in the construction of the equivariant fine-moduli families over the Hecke tower, namely by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuliT.exists_fineFamilyT_connected_value_of_fineFamily_of_towerFamily_of_isNoetherianRing_oneLegC5`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuliT.exists_fineFamilyT_connected_value_of_fineFamily_of_towerFamily_of_isNoetherianRing_oneLegC5) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_cerednikDrinfeld_fineFamily_value_of_connected_of_isNoetherianRing_equivariant_heightNormalised_conn`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_cerednikDrinfeld_fineFamily_value_of_connected_of_isNoetherianRing_equivariant_heightNormalised_conn).
